# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit. Real values live in .env; .env.example holds names only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and agent scaffolding
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradio. The launch writes a certificate and a flagging directory next to the
# app, and the share tunnel binary is downloaded rather than vendored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradio/
flagged/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated data. Rebuilt from the seed, never a source artifact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal
question_queue.duckdb

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results.
#
# The rule is not "results are noise". Some of it is evidence and some of it is
# live output, and the difference decides whether the demo works.
#
# LIVE CELL OUTPUT IS IGNORED, and that is load-bearing. The sweep resumes from
# results/sweep/. A committed cell would arrive on every clone and make the FIRST
# live sweep on a fresh machine resume-and-complete instantly, rendering finished
# numbers to a room told nothing is precomputed. A test asserts a fresh clone
# renders "not yet measured".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*.json
results/*.jsonl
# Derived, not evidence: build_gold memoises here, keyed on the warehouse seed plus a
# hash of gold/patterns.py and warehouse/semantic_model.yaml, so a rule edit invalidates
# it automatically. Committing it would ship an answer key nobody re-derived.
results/gold_cache.json
results/sweep/
results/ablation/
results/charts/
results/*.log
results/*.png
results/*.svg
results/_resume_marker*.txt

# Kept deliberately: the delivery reads reference cells for the frozen Sonnet
# measurements, and without them the DIAL chart has nothing to cite. This is
# also the only data tools/render_readme_charts.py is allowed to read.
!results/reference/

# Kept deliberately: the pre-fix measurements are the Stage 3 triage artifact —
# the under-specification we found in our own gold set and what it cost.
!results/prefix_v1/

# Kept deliberately: Gate 0 evidence, cited throughout the design record.
!results/gate0.json

# Kept deliberately: the determinism floor the pre-registration cites BY NAME before
# the first cell runs. It was ignored, so the citation resolved to nothing on every
# clone — a provenance line pointing at a file that was not there. Committing the file
# was the fix; a test now asserts every repo path named in sweep/ resolves on disk.
!results/noise_floor_*.json

# Kill-and-restart output, cited BY NAME in results/gate0.json as the evidence that
# LangSmith does not resume. Kept committed and kept un-ignored, deliberately.
#
# The exception is NOT removed, and that is the decision rather than an oversight. The
# log published a LangSmith organisation UUID and two more UUIDs in a public repo, so
# the identifiers are REDACTED IN PLACE — the finding, the date and the method survive
# and the identifiers do not. Deleting the file instead would have left gate0.json, which
# must not change, citing a path that no longer resolves: the same defect the lint rule
# and the pre-registration were both just fixed for. And a file that is tracked while
# ignored is a file whose future output silently never shows in git status.
!results/_resume_first.log
!results/_resume_marker.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# README images.
#
# assets/ IS committed — the README needs it on GitHub, and every file there is
# written by tools/render_readme_charts.py from results/reference/ and by
# nothing else. Anything that lands here by another route is a stray.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
assets/*
!assets/*.png
!assets/manifest.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging and backups
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.bundle
.hf-staging/
